      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: while we wait, here are some non-dancing examples for better clarify (I don't know why I didn't do that the first time!) \nDB-\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1L4sREEJJfa-HLQZMZGgyGsF5lqvTCfuY/view?usp=sharing\nPB-\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1hWROmoS3Bsy5IIa5D4FM0lLH8pJNjIul/view?usp=sharing\nIt's really weird. In the PB example, it's like the bones/colliders are almost completely being ignored on the left leg. I've tried this will immobile on 0 and 1 with no difference.\nAs you can see from the DB example, there is clipping at the extreme and almost unnatural angles, which is to be expected. But other than that, the colliders work smoothly and look fine in game.",
