      "value": "@{5f6e61f03043eb78f8fa3b88|full_name}: I'm not 100% sure what causes it but it may have some odd behaviour that is linked to the angle or direction of where you want the dynamics to move. When the collider is hit, i notice that the suction effect is turning at a specified angle and the suction effect may be amplified due to that. \nI feel like a quick fix could be to decouple the angle at which the dynamics move from the collider. When reducing the angle i noticed that the suction effect completely disappears however so does its ability to interact with colliders.",
