  "details": "VRChat Version: 2022.1.2p1, build 1190\nSDK: 2022.04.21.03.29_Public\n\nDescription of the bug: \nIt seems that the physbones colliders tend to clip through/ignore collision with physbones a lot easier than the old dynamic bones colliders.\n\nIt's VERY noticeable with clothes that collide with body parts, such as legs/skirts. Been trying a bevy of options using both simplified and advanced settings and can't seem to prevent clipping.\n\nFurther testing applied by placing individual PB components on each chain of the skirt instead of just one component on the root for a total of 16 separate PB components. A majority of the components ignored collision while others worked fine.\n\nOne additional curveball is that it seems to happen at random, but more so on the noticeable side.\nI've added 3 images.\n\n1: Doesn't collide with PB on skirt root\n2: Collides with PB on individual skirt chain\n3: Doesn't collide with PB on individual skirt chain\n\n(updated subject and added more results)",
